   of Data (CoDS-COMAD), Kolkata, INDIA, JAN 03-05, 2019},
Abstract = {With the increase in user generated content, particularly on social
   media networks, the amount of hate speech is also steadily increasing.
   So, there is a need to automatically detect such hateful content and
   curb the wrongful activities. While relevant research has been done
   independently on code-mixed social media texts and hate speech
   detection, this paper deals with the task of identification of hate
   speech from code-mixed social media text. We perform experiments with
   available code-mixed dataset for hate speech detection using two
   architectures namely sub-word level LSTM model and Hierarchical LSTM
   model with attention based on phonemic sub-words.},
