   Offensive Language Detection in Social Media},
Booktitle = {PROCEEDINGS OF THE FOURTEENTH WORKSHOP ON SEMANTIC EVALUATION},
Year = {2020},
Pages = {1516-1523},
Note = {14th International Workshops on Semantic Evaluation (SemEval), ELECTR
   NETWORK, DEC 12-13, 2020},
Organization = {ACL Special Interest Grp Lexicon},
Abstract = {This paper describes the systems our team (AdelaideCyC) has developed
   for SemEval Task 12 (OffensEval 2020) to detect offensive language in
   social media. The challenge focuses on three subtasks - offensive
   language identification (subtask A), offense type identification
   (subtask B), and offense target identification (subtask C). Our team has
   participated in all the three subtasks. We have developed machine
   learning and deep learning-based ensembles of models. We have achieved
   F1-scores of 0.906, 0.552, and 0.623 in subtask A, B, and C
   respectively. While our performance scores are promising for subtask A,
   the results demonstrate that subtask B and C still remain challenging to
   classify.},
