   Information Systems (NLDB), Paris, FRANCE, JUN 13-15, 2018},
Abstract = {Hate speech may take different forms in online social media. Most of the
   investigations in the literature are focused on detecting abusive
   language in discussions about ethnicity, religion, gender identity and
   sexual orientation. In this paper, we address the problem of automatic
   detection and categorization of misogynous language in online social
   media. The main contribution of this paper is two-fold: (1) a corpus of
   misogynous tweets, labelled from different perspective and (2) an
   exploratory investigations on NLP features and ML models for detecting
   and classifying misogynistic language.},
