Abstract = {In this paper, we address the offensive language detection on Tamazight
   language, which is one of the under-resourced languages that are still
   in their infancy and lack of standard orthography. We are particularly
   interested in the Kabyle dialect, mainly spoken in some cities of
   northern Algeria (i.e. Tizi-ouzou and Bejaia). We propose a new corpus
   of offensive Tamazight language (i.e. OTAM corpus) compiling 6.2k texts,
   as well as a new lexicon of offensive and abusive Tamazight words with
   12.6k entries. We have evaluated several baseline classifiers of machine
   learning and deep learning, where the results showed that we could
   produce acceptable results without features engineering.},
