   Interaction Institute},
Abstract = {Trolling behavior in online games is a persistent issue that disrupts
   user experience or player enjoyment, and even leads to player churn.
   This paper proposes a deep learning-based method for detecting
   intentional toxic behavior, with a particular focus on griefing, by
   utilizing in-game telemetry data from PlayerUnknown's Battlegrounds
   (PUBG). Using behavioral patterns aggregated from a two-month data
   collection period, our model achieves strong anomaly detection
   performance while remaining interpretable for developers by anomaly
   score. We validate our approach through experimental analysis and expert
   feedback.},
